From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: 992 - grace before evicting an MLO client

wifi_sta_periodic_run polls wifi.apmld every 1s for affiliated APs and, on an
empty reply, immediately wifi_del_sta()'d the MLO client -- zero grace, while
the legacy path tolerates STA_STALE_STATS_CNT_MAX(60) stale ticks. wifi.apmld
is racy/often-empty, so a single bad snapshot evicted a still-connected MLO
client from ap->stalist (and stamldlist) until the 60s async refresh re-added
it, under-reporting it to the controller the whole time. Give the MLO path the
same grace: count stale ticks and only evict past the threshold; reset on a
good reply. Genuine disconnects still come through the assoc/disassoc event.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/agent.c
+++ b/src/agent.c
@@ -1498,18 +1498,29 @@
 			goto rearm_periodic;
 
 		if (hwaddr_is_zero(mlsta.sta[0].macaddr)) {
-			uint8_t macaddr[6];
+			/* 992: an empty apmld reply is usually a transient race (the
+			 * per-STA timer polls the flaky wifi.apmld every 1s), not a
+			 * real disconnect. Give the MLO client the same grace as the
+			 * legacy path instead of evicting on one bad snapshot, which
+			 * under-reports it to the controller for up to a full async
+			 * refresh interval. A genuine disconnect still arrives via the
+			 * assoc/disassoc event; this is only the safety-net poll. */
+			if (s->stale_stats_cnt++ > STA_STALE_STATS_CNT_MAX) {
+				uint8_t macaddr[6];
 
-			dbg("%s: sta:"MACFMT" is no longer connected\n",
-			    __func__, MAC2STR(s->macaddr));
+				dbg("%s: sta:"MACFMT" is no longer connected\n",
+				    __func__, MAC2STR(s->macaddr));
 
-			memcpy(macaddr, s->macaddr, 6);
-			wifi_topology_notification(a, s, ap,
-					0x00 /* left */,
-					0x01 /* unspecified reason */);
-			wifi_del_sta(a, ap->ifname, macaddr);
-			return;
+				memcpy(macaddr, s->macaddr, 6);
+				wifi_topology_notification(a, s, ap,
+						0x00 /* left */,
+						0x01 /* unspecified reason */);
+				wifi_del_sta(a, ap->ifname, macaddr);
+				return;
+			}
+			goto rearm_periodic;
 		}
+		s->stale_stats_cnt = 0;	/* found: reset grace counter */
 
 		if (mlsta.mlo_capable == true &&
 		    !hwaddr_is_zero(mlsta.sta[0].bssid))
